node-corepack (0.36.0+ds-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.36.0.
  * Independent local repackaging of upstream v0.36.0, modelled on the
    conventions of Debian's node-corepack source package (Debian
    infrastructure was unreachable from this build environment, so this
    packaging was written from scratch rather than derived from the
    js-team packaging).
  * Repack upstream tarball (+ds): exclude tests/nocks.db, a 57 MB
    binary HTTP-fixture database only used by the test suite.
  * debian/rules: standalone makefile build (no debhelper) so the
    package builds on minimal systems; bundles sources with esbuild and
    generates the dist entry scripts the same way upstream mkshims.ts
    does. Note: devDependencies are fetched from the npm registry at
    build time, so this source package is NOT suitable for upload to
    the Debian archive as-is (archive builds must be offline).
  * Apply upstream's clipanion "main" field fix
    (.yarn/patches/clipanion-npm-3.2.1-fc9187f56c.patch) to the
    npm-fetched clipanion before bundling, matching upstream's build.
  * Test suite disabled: it requires network access and the excluded
    fixture database.

 -- Antony <antony@beyonk.com>  Tue, 09 Sep 2026 12:20:00 +0000
